<!-- ─── About Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="about-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">About the Project</span>
    <h1 class="page-title">Preserving Knowledge, One QR Code at a Time</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">
      The Dangcagan National High School Digital Herbarium bridges traditional Philippine
      herbal medicine knowledge with modern technology — making plant information accessible
      to students, teachers, and the community through a simple scan.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── Mission ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container two-col">
    <div class="reveal" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Our Mission</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Knowledge that grows with the garden</h2>
      <p>
        The Dangcagan National High School Digital Herbarium was created to preserve and share
        the rich botanical heritage of Philippine medicinal plants. By pairing physical specimens
        in our school garden with QR-coded digital records, we make centuries of folk knowledge
        instantly accessible to anyone with a smartphone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each plant entry is researched and curated by students and faculty, documenting not just
        the plant's identity, but also its medicinal uses, traditional preparation methods,
        cultivation requirements, and important safety precautions. The collection prioritizes
        the ten medicinal plants officially endorsed by the Philippine Department of Health.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" data-reveal>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-icon">
          <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2L4 7v10l8 5 8-5V7z"/><path d="M12 22V12"/><path d="M4 7l8 5 8-5"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Educational Access</h3>
        <p>Every QR code on a physical plant links directly to a digital record — bringing textbook-quality information into the garden itself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

